    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "bd5e2b8af38ef8c32df874f42881894c6c633cf4bce579ff4bdcb48434091278",
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel.\n\nIn the morning, visit the Orongo Ceremonial Center. The excursion begins with a climb along the slopes of Rano Kau Volcano to a viewpoint on the edge of the crater, where a lake lies amid distinctive vegetation. Continue to the Ceremonial Village of Orongo, where the island's leader was chosen for a one-year term through a challenging and dangerous competition. Each spring, the island's clans gathered in stone houses and waited for the arrival of the sacred Manutara bird before choosing the Tangata Manu, or Birdman.\n\nDuration of the morning excursion: about 4 hours.\n\nIn the afternoon, explore the central part of Easter Island, including Ahu Akivi, a platform with seven Moai statues. The site is linked to the legend of the arrival of the Polynesian people on the island. Unlike most Moai, these statues face toward the sea.\n\nContinue to Puna Pau Quarry, a small volcanic hill where red stone was extracted to make the Moai headpieces. The site offers a viewpoint overlooking Hanga Roa.\n\nDuration of the afternoon excursion: about 4 hours.\n\n**Meals:** breakfast.",
